      `liability is otherwise admitted`               IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`General Condition 7 — the difference must be referred to arbitration` `the difference is about the amount to be paid` `liability is otherwise admitted` MEANS
        `the difference is about the amount to be paid`
    AND `liability is otherwise admitted`

-- Failing a single arbitrator agreed by both, each party appoints one in writing within one
-- month of the other's written request. Read as a calendar month from the day the request
-- is sent (fork F15). The clause states no consequence of a failure to appoint and no other
-- way to constitute the tribunal (finding X8).
